<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-memory-04--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-memory-04: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.12";
    dc:description "Mnemonic improvisation is offered as one kind of cognitive glue that reifies Selves. Coupling, shared dynamics, and information flow are non-cognitive descriptions of the same multi-scale organization, and no public observation picks the glue account out from those rivals. The proposal stays conceptual.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Remapping of stored information onto a new context can be measured in particular systems, but success or failure of remapping would not show that this capacity is what binds parts into a Self.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Self is not given an operational boundary distinct from physiological or informational coupling.", "The claim quantifies over every scale, from cells to organisms.";
